# The gateway's documentation as a collection of mcp-docs
# (https://github.com/sdrahn/mcp-docs): an agent that runs mcp-docs
# itself, without the gateway, reads it as the collection mcp-gateway.
# Installed with the documentation; it does nothing without mcp-docs. To
# change it, copy it to /etc/mcp-docs/collections.d/mcp-gateway.yaml; an
# empty file of that name disables it.
title: mcp-gateway documentation
root: @DATADIR@/mcp-gateway/docs
description: >
  The MCP gateway, for the installed version: user guide (13 chapters),
  architecture and decisions, changelog with upgrade notes.
index: README.md
instructions: >
  Read architecture.md and CHANGELOG.md by section, never whole. The
  configuration on this machine is not here: through the gateway, the
  server gateway-admin shows it (show_config) and checks it
  (check_config, doctor); on the machine, mcp-gateway-admin doctor.
